dns — provenance note
======================

Kept as a module-local NOTICE (same placement as the sibling `ocsp`/`rdap`/
`whois` modules, which document the same live-capture reasoning).

Provenance
----------

dns — clean-room implementation from RFC 1035 (message format), RFC 2782
(SRV), RFC 3596 (AAAA/reverse), RFC 8484 (DoH) and RFC 8659 (CAA), modeled
after the public behavior of Go's `net`/`x/net/dns/dnsmessage` and
miekg/dns (see the module doc comments) — no third-party source was ported
or copied.

`modules/dns/src/goldens.zig` (added 2026-08-01) holds six real DNS
responses captured live from Google Public DNS (`8.8.8.8`): `example.com`
A/AAAA/TXT, a real `www.wikipedia.org` CNAME chain, a real `iana.org` MX
answer set, and a real NXDOMAIN with its authority-section SOA — see that
file's own doc comment for the exact capture recipe and what each response
exercises that the hand-built goldens in `message.zig` do not (principally:
real-server name-compression pointer placement).

Attribution for the captured responses: NONE required, by the same
reasoning `ocsp`'s `NOTICE` gives for its live CA captures (root NOTICE §0's
black-box-oracle relationship): no third-party source or design was
consulted, only the observable wire output of a public resolver answering a
stock RFC 1035 query — protocol structure (dictated by the RFC) plus facts
(IP addresses, TTLs, already-published hostnames), not copyrightable
expression. No root NOTICE change accompanies this addition.

No GPL/LGPL/AGPL source was consulted or copied anywhere in this module.
